## Common Failures and Fixes

| Symptom | Cause | Fix |
|---------|-------|-----|
| `EntityAlreadyExists: Role with name northstar-dev-MLEngineer` / `BucketAlreadyOwnedByYou` on apply | Part A not torn down | Step 0.1; Part A teardown in [[Lab_1a--Solution Notes (Manual Steps)]] |
| `terraform init`: `S3 bucket "northstar-tfstate-YOUR_ACCOUNT_ID" does not exist` or `NoSuchBucket` | `bootstrap-state.sh` not run, or run from the wrong directory (it patches a relative path) | Run it from the repo root; confirm `backend.tf` has a 12-digit ID |
| `terraform init`: "Backend configuration changed… migrate?" | Local state from an earlier `init` | Answer `yes`, or `terraform init -migrate-state` |
| Domain `Creating…` > 15 min, then `ValidationException … service-linked role` | Missing `AWSServiceRoleForAmazonSageMakerNotebooks` | Step 0.4; then `terraform apply` again — state resumes |
| `InvalidParameterValue: … description … ` on the security group | Non-ASCII character (em dash) in `description` | ASCII only. `validate` and LocalStack do not catch this |
| `ValidationException` on `jupyter_server_app_settings` instance type | `var.instance_type` used where `"system"` is required | Step 4 |
| `terraform destroy` hangs 10 min on `aws_subnet.public` / `aws_security_group.this`, then `DependencyViolation` | No `retention_policy { home_efs_file_system = "Delete" }` → EFS mount target pins the subnet | Add it for next time. Now: EFS console → filesystem tagged `ManagedByAmazonSageMakerResource` → delete mount targets → delete filesystem → delete the two `security-group-for-*-nfs-d-*` SGs → `terraform destroy` again |
| Destroy fails on `aws_sagemaker_user_profile`: apps still `InService` | JupyterLab space left running | Stop it (Step 17 check); wait for `list-apps` empty; destroy again |
| `terraform destroy` → `BucketNotEmpty` | `force_destroy` omitted | Add it, `terraform apply` (updates in place), destroy again. Or empty the bucket including versions by hand |
| Second `terraform plan` shows a change on the Domain every time | Missing `studio_web_portal_settings {}` | Step 4; apply once more, plan goes to "No changes" |
| `Error acquiring the state lock` … `ConditionalCheckFailedException` | Previous run was killed mid-write (Ctrl-C twice, closed laptop) | `terraform force-unlock <ID from the error>` — only after confirming no other apply is running |
| `verify-lab1.sh`: `ERROR: Run 'terraform apply' … first` | Run from inside `environments/dev`, or destroy already ran | Run from repo root, while the stack is up |
| `verify-lab1.sh`: `B2 apply output shows Apply complete` fails | apply not captured with `tee`, or captured to the wrong path | Step 16 — path is relative to `environments/dev`: `../../../docs/` |
| `verify-lab1.sh`: `B4 No hardcoded 'northstar' literals` fails | `"northstar-dev-data-*"` in the IAM policy, or a bucket name string | Build it from `var.project`/`var.environment` + `aws_caller_identity` (Step 3) |
| `verify-lab1.sh`: `A3 IAM sim: MLEngineer DENIED write to raw/` fails (`allowed`) | S3 object statement on `${bucket_arn}/*` or `s3:*` | Scope to `/artifacts/*` and `/features/*` only |
| Studio page: "Permissions not configured correctly" | `StudioSelfService` statement missing | Step 3; `terraform apply` updates the policy in place, reload Studio |
| `make local-validate`: `Cannot connect to the Docker daemon` | Docker Desktop not running | Start it, re-run |
| `make local-validate`: `dial tcp 127.0.0.1:4566: connection refused` | LocalStack not healthy yet, or port in use | `docker compose ps` (should be `healthy`); `lsof -i :4566` for a squatter |
| `make local-validate`: `awslocal: command not found` | Not installed, or installed off `PATH` | `pipx install awscli-local` |
| LocalStack output shows `172.31.0.0/16` and six subnets | LocalStack's emulated default VPC | Expected; rubric ignores it. The student's `10.0.0.0/16` should also be there |
| `check-secrets.sh` flags `AKIAIOSFODNN7EXAMPLE` | Student is running an old `git log -S AKIA` from a stale kit | Use the shipped script; it whitelists AWS's placeholder |
| `Warning: Deprecated Parameter "dynamodb_table"` on every command | Terraform ≥ 1.11 | Harmless. Keep `dynamodb_table` — the rubric grades the lock table (Phase 3 note) |
| `terraform fmt -check` fails on a file that "looks fine" | `=` alignment, trailing whitespace, tabs | `terraform fmt -recursive infrastructure/` and commit |